# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# BustedLab configuration.
#
# Every variable the code reads is listed here, grouped by what breaks
# without it, with the real failure mode rather than "required: yes". The
# ones that FAIL CLOSED are the security-critical ones: the feature they
# guard simply refuses to work when they are unset, which is deliberate and
# is not a bug to work around.
#
# Copy to .env.local for development. In production these live in the Vercel
# project's environment variables.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ── 1. WITHOUT THESE, THE PRODUCT DOES NOT WORK ────────────────────────

# Upstash Redis. Free-scan limits, sessions, the scan ledger, the
# leaderboards, the identity cache and the model spend budget all live here.
# Unset: every read fails open, so the site still serves, but nothing is
# counted, nothing is limited and nothing is remembered.
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# Claude. This is the identification gate - the thing that decides what a
# photo shows. Unset: every candidate comes back unverified, so no scan can
# ever produce a confident verdict.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Product search. SerpApi drives Google Lens (reverse image), Google
# Shopping, and the direct-retailer engines (Amazon, Walmart, eBay). Serper
# is the cheaper backup for Lens and Shopping only.
# Unset: no candidates to identify, so every scan is UNRESOLVED. At least
# one is required; SerpApi alone is a working configuration, Serper alone is
# a degraded one (no direct-retailer layer).
SERPAPI_KEY=
SERPER_API_KEY=

# Vercel Blob. Google Lens can only be handed a URL, so the uploaded photo
# is briefly published to an unguessable one and deleted the moment the
# reverse-image call returns.
# Unset: the Lens layer is skipped entirely and identification falls back to
# text search, which is the accuracy the whole v10 rewrite exists to beat.
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=

# The canonical origin, no trailing slash. Sign-in links, the access email,
# robots.txt and sitemap.xml all build on it.
# Unset: sign-in links are REFUSED on any host this app does not own (see
# getBaseUrl in src/app/api/auth/route.ts), and the purchase email is not
# sent at all. Set it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://bustedlab.com


# ── 2. WITHOUT THESE, THE PRIVACY POLICY IS NOT TRUE ───────────────────

# The salt for one-way IP and email hashes. The policy states that IP
# addresses are stored only as salted one-way hashes; with the built-in
# fallback salt that sentence is technically true and practically empty,
# because the whole IPv4 space can be hashed against a known salt in
# seconds. A real random value is what makes the claim mean anything.
#   openssl rand -hex 32
IDENTITY_SALT=

# Signs the unsubscribe links in product update emails. Those links never
# expire, so this must never change once list mail has gone out. Optional:
# without it IDENTITY_SALT is used, but then rotating IDENTITY_SALT breaks
# every unsubscribe link already sent. Set it before the first send.
#   openssl rand -hex 32
UNSUBSCRIBE_SECRET=

# Signs /api/proxy-image URLs so the route only ever fetches an image the
# engine itself chose to show. Without it the route falls back to
# IDENTITY_SALT and then to a built-in development value; a built-in default
# is derivable by anyone who can read the source, so this is what actually
# closes the "free image CDN billed to us" hole.
# Rotating it is safe: stored proxy paths are re-signed as they are read, so
# no permanent scan page loses its photo.
#   openssl rand -hex 32
IMAGE_PROXY_SECRET=


# ── 3. WITHOUT THESE, THE BUSINESS CANNOT TAKE MONEY ───────────────────

# The live payment link, and the single source of truth for checkout. A
# Lemon Squeezy link opens as an in-page overlay; any other provider's link
# opens as a full-page checkout.
#   https://<store>.lemonsqueezy.com/checkout/buy/<variant-id>
# Use the LIVE-mode link. See LEMONSQUEEZY_ACCEPT_TEST_ORDERS below for what
# happens to test-mode purchases in production.
#
# Checkout stays OFFLINE (503, "Checkout offline" in the UI) unless it is
# safe to take money: this link is set, PAYMENT_PROVIDER does not contradict
# it, and the matching webhook secret below is set. A purchase the webhook
# cannot verify is a customer charged and never given access, so the button
# refuses rather than allowing it. The exact reason is written to the server
# log on every request while it is offline.
CHECKOUT_URL=

# gumroad | lemonsqueezy | paddle. LEAVE UNSET: the provider is read from
# CHECKOUT_URL's domain. Set it only for a custom checkout domain the link
# alone cannot identify.
#
# This used to show PAYMENT_PROVIDER=gumroad here, which was a trap: with a
# Lemon Squeezy link and that value, every purchase was charged and then
# rejected by the webhook. A value that contradicts the link now keeps
# checkout offline instead, and the webhook no longer reads this at all - it
# identifies each delivery by its own signature header.
PAYMENT_PROVIDER=

# Webhook signing secrets. ALL PATHS FAIL CLOSED: with no secret configured,
# no delivery of that kind is ever trusted, because anyone who can POST to
# the webhook would otherwise be able to grant themselves lifetime access.
#
# Lemon Squeezy: Settings > Webhooks, endpoint https://<your-domain>/api/webhook,
# events order_created and order_refunded, and a signing secret of your
# choosing, which goes here. If the store keeps separate test-mode and
# live-mode webhooks, give both the same secret.
LEMONSQUEEZY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
GUMROAD_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Optional hardening for Gumroad. Without the permalink, ANY sale from this
# seller unlocks BustedLab, including a different product.
GUMROAD_SELLER_ID=
GUMROAD_PRODUCT_PERMALINK=
PADDLE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Keeping a previous provider's secret set after moving is deliberate and
# useful: its refunds and chargebacks can still revoke access.

# Test-mode Lemon Squeezy orders are paid for with the processor's published
# test cards. On the PRODUCTION deployment they are verified, logged, and NOT
# granted - otherwise a CHECKOUT_URL left pointing at a test-mode product
# gives permanent access to anyone who types 4242 4242 4242 4242. Set this to
# true for the length of an end-to-end test on production, then remove it.
# Preview and local deployments accept test orders without it.
LEMONSQUEEZY_ACCEPT_TEST_ORDERS=

# Transactional email: the access email after purchase and the sign-in link.
# Unset: access is still granted on purchase, but the customer has to use
# the sign-in form to reach it and never receives a link.
RESEND_API_KEY=


# ── 4. WITHOUT THESE, TWO ENDPOINTS ARE SEALED SHUT ────────────────────
# Both FAIL CLOSED on purpose. Unset means "nobody gets in", never "everybody".

# Authorises the daily blob-cleanup cron. Vercel sends it automatically as a
# bearer token when set on the project.
CRON_SECRET=

# Bearer token for GET /api/stats, the only non-public endpoint on the site.
# Scan volume, verdict mix and conversion are the numbers a competitor would
# most like to have.
ANALYTICS_TOKEN=


# ── 5. COST AND ABUSE CONTROLS (optional, defaults shown) ──────────────
# These are the dials that decide what a viral day costs. See
# scripts/cost-model.mjs for the arithmetic behind the defaults, and
# src/lib/model-budget.ts for what happens when the budget is reached.

# Daily ceiling on Claude spend, in USD, measured from the usage the API
# reports rather than estimated. Past it the engine DEGRADES rather than
# failing: cheap gate, cache-first, enhancement layers dropped, strongest
# label withheld. A scan still answers.
DAILY_MODEL_BUDGET_USD=250

# How long the engine stays degraded after the API pushes back with a 429,
# 402 or 529, in seconds.
MODEL_BREAKER_COOLDOWN=300

# Uncached scans per day across all free users. A second bound, denominated
# in scans rather than dollars. Note that it does NOT apply to paid
# accounts, which is why the dollar budget above is the real ceiling.
GLOBAL_DAILY_SCAN_CAP=25000

# Per-IP burst limits.
SCAN_BURST_PER_MINUTE=12
EVENT_BURST_PER_MINUTE=60
# Break-glass switch for the Content-Security-Policy, which is enforced on
# every page (src/lib/csp.ts). "true" sends the same policy as report-only
# so nothing is blocked while a fix for a wrongly blocked resource ships.
# Leave unset.
CSP_REPORT_ONLY=

# Product update sign-ups accepted per IP per hour, so a script cannot fill
# the list with addresses that never agreed to it.
NOTIFY_PER_IP_PER_HOUR=5

# Fair-use ceiling on the unlimited paid tier, per account per UTC day. Paid
# accounts bypass the free allowance and GLOBAL_DAILY_SCAN_CAP, so before this
# existed one leaked or scripted session could spend roughly $800 of model and
# search budget in a day. At 500 it is roughly $25, and no real customer is
# near it. Disclosed in the terms page, so changing it means changing that
# text too.
PAID_DAILY_SCAN_CEILING=500

# How long a confirmed identification is reused across users, in seconds.
# This is the single biggest cost lever during a spike; shortening it trades
# money for freshness of the source price.
IDENTITY_CACHE_TTL=3600
